// Probe 06 — Cluster I variant: nested `(vec[i] ?? "a") ?? "b"` chain
//
// Tests whether chaining `??` operators stacks the broken pattern.  The
// inner `vec[i] ?? "a"` builds a `_ncc_N` block; the outer `?? "b"` then
// sees a "non-trivial" LHS (the inner Block expression) and builds
// ANOTHER `_ncc_M` block on top.
//
// Two failure modes to look for:
//   1. Inner block returns dangling Str (cluster I) → outer block reads it
//      and may either propagate corruption OR mask it by re-allocating.
//   2. Outer block has its own freed-then-read pattern (cluster I^2).
//
// Expected (rustc 1.96 / macOS): probably FAIL on --interpret.  If 06
// passes while 02 fails, the outer `_ncc_M` allocation incidentally
// materialises bytes that escape the inner block's free — interesting
// edge case for the fix.
// Pairing: diff against 02 to see if nesting changes the symptom.
// Status: cluster I variant probe.

struct H { items: vector<text> }

fn main() {
  h = H { items: [] };
  h.items += ["present"];
  a = (h.items[0] ?? "a") ?? "b";
  assert(a == "present", "probe 06: got '{a}', want 'present'");
  println("probe 06 PASSED");
}
